  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 101 AM EDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nNext week will continue to be unsettled across the region. The upper \nlevel low will eventually lift to the northeast and get absorbed in \nthe broader upper level flow early in the work week, however a \nribbon of enhanced moisture will continue to stream across South FL \nfor much of the week. This will result in PoPs remaining above \nnormal (70-90%) through the end of the work week, with the highest \nchances being during the afternoon and early evening hours each day. \nUrban and poor drainage flooding will remain a concern each, with \nWPC maintaining a marginal risk of excessive rainfall over the metro \neach day through day 5. \n\nWith the expected rainfall and cloud cover each day, temps will \nhover right around normal next week with highs generally in the \nupper 80s to around 90. Low temps will range from the lower 70s over \nthe interior to mid and upper 70s closer to the coasts.",
